WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.869 --> 00:00:02.930
- Good morning, Believe
Nation, today's message is

00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:05.537
don't live in the past.

00:00:05.537 --> 00:00:07.859
Over to you, Anthony Hopkins.

00:00:07.859 --> 00:00:09.879
(rooster crowing)

00:00:09.879 --> 00:00:12.706
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:12.706 --> 00:00:14.956
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:14.956 --> 00:00:18.456
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:19.473 --> 00:00:20.643
- [Woman] Your approach to life,

00:00:20.643 --> 00:00:23.236
has it changed through
your acting experience?

00:00:23.236 --> 00:00:26.764
- Yes, whether you just get
older, if you live long enough,

00:00:26.764 --> 00:00:30.759
you'll change; and if you
don't, you may as well die.

00:00:30.759 --> 00:00:32.540
(laughter)

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:35.873
You know, go or grow, you have to change

00:00:37.112 --> 00:00:39.904
and I've realized over the
years that I've gone through

00:00:39.904 --> 00:00:41.904
many changes in my life.

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:46.732
Many changes because
that's the nature of life

00:00:46.732 --> 00:00:50.494
and if you don't go with it,
you may as well not breathe,

00:00:50.494 --> 00:00:51.965
you may as well be dead.

00:00:51.965 --> 00:00:53.421
I know people who live in the past,

00:00:53.421 --> 00:00:55.759
they just live back there all the time,

00:00:55.759 --> 00:00:58.152
talking about something that
happened to them 30 years ago,

00:00:58.152 --> 00:01:01.576
they're like zombies and I can't
hang out with those people.

00:01:01.576 --> 00:01:04.004
I know them, but I can't
spend more than five minutes

00:01:04.004 --> 00:01:05.894
with them because I feel
like suicide at the end of it

00:01:05.894 --> 00:01:07.537
because I feel so guilty

00:01:07.537 --> 00:01:09.599
about being happy when
they're so miserable.

00:01:09.599 --> 00:01:11.997
(laughter)

00:01:11.997 --> 00:01:14.015
You know, life is in session.

00:01:14.015 --> 00:01:16.068
For many years, I thought
life was a big rehearsal

00:01:16.068 --> 00:01:19.188
for the big event and
somebody in Los Angeles said,

00:01:19.188 --> 00:01:23.464
"Tony, this is the big
event, life is in session."

00:01:23.464 --> 00:01:25.582
You know, we spend so much
time thinking it's a rehearsal

00:01:25.582 --> 00:01:29.582
for the big event, the
big red carpet in the sky

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:31.997
and it's not.

00:01:31.997 --> 00:01:34.243
- So this is an interesting one for me.

00:01:34.243 --> 00:01:35.855
First, I think too many
people live in the past,

00:01:35.855 --> 00:01:39.189
I think too many people are
living off of their past glory

00:01:39.189 --> 00:01:42.047
or are living through other people, right?

00:01:42.047 --> 00:01:44.006
Like they didn't have a lot
of success so they're living

00:01:44.006 --> 00:01:45.908
through their kids and
the only value they get

00:01:45.908 --> 00:01:48.127
is when their kids go
off and do something.

00:01:48.127 --> 00:01:50.340
I think that is just fundamentally broken.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:51.589
Yes, you love your kids.

00:01:51.589 --> 00:01:54.354
Yes, you love the people
around you, but it's your life.

00:01:54.354 --> 00:01:56.924
You got to do the thing that
you want to go out and do

00:01:56.924 --> 00:01:59.807
and stop just telling stories
of what happened before.

00:01:59.807 --> 00:02:03.371
Stop reliving what happened
five, 10, 20 years ago

00:02:03.371 --> 00:02:06.426
and now is the time to go
out and do something amazing.

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:09.218
This may seem really bad
but I was reading the book

00:02:09.218 --> 00:02:12.798
this morning and one
of the exercises in it

00:02:12.798 --> 00:02:16.923
was around rewiring your
brain and so the concept here

00:02:16.923 --> 00:02:18.525
is whether you're feeling down

00:02:18.525 --> 00:02:21.020
or whether you're feeling
happy, you can rewire your brain

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:22.913
to feel the opposite if you want to.

00:02:22.913 --> 00:02:24.983
So if you're feeling down you
can take that negative thought

00:02:24.983 --> 00:02:28.023
you have and you picture it
and you see it as this big

00:02:28.023 --> 00:02:31.714
overwhelming huge thing in
your life and then eventually

00:02:31.714 --> 00:02:34.106
you look at it and it's
getting smaller and further off

00:02:34.106 --> 00:02:36.571
in the distance, and smaller
and smaller and smaller

00:02:36.571 --> 00:02:39.077
and smaller until it kind
of fades off into the sun.

00:02:39.077 --> 00:02:41.954
You wake up, you open your
eyes, you feel happier.

00:02:41.954 --> 00:02:44.490
You can do it the other
way to feel happier

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:45.872
by looking at positive things.

00:02:45.872 --> 00:02:48.413
Take on really positive
memory that you have

00:02:48.413 --> 00:02:50.736
and just make it big, make
it bigger in your life

00:02:50.736 --> 00:02:52.550
and brighter and more in your face

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:54.962
and feel the happiness that comes from it.

00:02:54.962 --> 00:02:56.923
I just thought it was an
interesting exercise to test

00:02:56.923 --> 00:02:59.931
and when I first read
about it, I had a hard time

00:02:59.931 --> 00:03:03.348
thinking about one defining happy moment,

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:07.553
which sounds really sad,
but it wasn't sad for me

00:03:07.553 --> 00:03:10.610
because I don't live in the past.

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:12.148
I don't remember how old I am.

00:03:12.148 --> 00:03:14.308
You know, when I get asked on
those forms how old are you?

00:03:14.308 --> 00:03:15.975
I have to think about what
year is it, when was I born,

00:03:15.975 --> 00:03:18.423
and make the calculation.

00:03:18.423 --> 00:03:21.350
When people ask me when did
I start my YouTube channel,

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:24.344
how long have I been in the YouTube world?

00:03:24.344 --> 00:03:27.005
I don't know, who cares?

00:03:27.005 --> 00:03:29.285
Like, I don't care when I
started, I care what I'm doing

00:03:29.285 --> 00:03:31.666
right now, I care where we're
going, I care about the impact

00:03:31.666 --> 00:03:35.448
that I want to have, not
what I did years ago.

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:37.589
I legitimately don't remember.

00:03:37.589 --> 00:03:40.039
Unless it's part of the story,
the narrative of lessons

00:03:40.039 --> 00:03:41.906
that I've learned that
I don't want to forget,

00:03:41.906 --> 00:03:44.247
or that could be teachable
moments for you guys,

00:03:44.247 --> 00:03:46.138
I don't remember that stuff.

00:03:46.138 --> 00:03:48.458
All the milestones that
we hit, I don't know.

00:03:48.458 --> 00:03:49.575
When did we hit 100,000?

00:03:49.575 --> 00:03:50.579
I have no idea.

00:03:50.579 --> 00:03:54.488
How long did it take me to
get 1,000, 10,000, 100,000?

00:03:54.488 --> 00:03:56.686
Even now, I don't know how long it took.

00:03:56.686 --> 00:03:58.301
Who cares, why does that matter?

00:03:58.301 --> 00:03:59.797
How is that relevant?

00:03:59.797 --> 00:04:01.450
I want to be happy with
what I'm doing right now

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:04.132
and make something great
going forward and so I

00:04:04.132 --> 00:04:08.387
have trouble thinking of one
defining moment of happiness

00:04:08.387 --> 00:04:10.345
as like, the one happy moment in my life

00:04:10.345 --> 00:04:13.021
because I want today to be happy.

00:04:13.021 --> 00:04:14.825
I want today to be the happiest day.

00:04:14.825 --> 00:04:16.708
I want tomorrow to be the happiest day.

00:04:16.708 --> 00:04:18.775
Maybe I'm just a weird bird that way

00:04:18.775 --> 00:04:22.030
'cause I know a lot of people,
that's what they live off of,

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:23.833
is like, it took me this long to get here

00:04:23.833 --> 00:04:26.318
and they remember all the
dates and all the milestones.

00:04:26.318 --> 00:04:29.096
I don't know, let's turn that
into the question of the day.

00:04:29.096 --> 00:04:32.927
Am I the weird bird or do
you gusy feel the same way?

00:04:32.927 --> 00:04:35.359
Are you living in the past,
do you remember every detail,

00:04:35.359 --> 00:04:37.648
every moment, and you're not happy now,

00:04:37.648 --> 00:04:41.137
or are you focused on being
happy with what you're doing

00:04:41.137 --> 00:04:43.872
today and going forward, or
maybe you found the creative way

00:04:43.872 --> 00:04:47.328
to embrace the genius
of the and and do both.

00:04:47.328 --> 00:04:49.097
Let me know what you think.

00:04:49.097 --> 00:04:51.736
Are you living in the past or not?

00:04:51.736 --> 00:04:54.384
Leave it in the comments below,
super curious to find out.

00:04:54.384 --> 00:04:57.193
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Tim Murphy

00:04:57.193 --> 00:04:58.333
from cleverrestaurantconsulting.com.

00:04:58.333 --> 00:05:00.689
Tim, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:05:00.689 --> 00:05:03.098
Your One Word, it really
means a lot to me, man,

00:05:03.098 --> 00:05:04.159
I appreciate it.

00:05:04.159 --> 00:05:06.699
Thank you guys again for
watching, I believe in you.

00:05:06.699 --> 00:05:08.608
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:10.853
and whatever your one word is.

00:05:10.853 --> 00:05:13.014
Much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:05:13.014 --> 00:05:15.482
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:05:15.482 --> 00:05:18.575
♫ I wake up every morning

00:05:18.575 --> 00:05:21.993
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:05:21.993 --> 00:05:24.352
Hey Believe Nation, for those
of you who want a little bit

00:05:24.352 --> 00:05:27.740
more context and value around
not living in the past,

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:31.767
here are a few more bonus clips
that I think you'll enjoy.

00:05:31.767 --> 00:05:33.661
Most people have good, great goals.

00:05:33.661 --> 00:05:35.096
I want to increase my
income and lose weight

00:05:35.096 --> 00:05:37.325
and get out of debt and be
thin and happy and healthy

00:05:37.325 --> 00:05:40.631
and have a wonderful family,
but then, then they decide

00:05:40.631 --> 00:05:43.869
but before I start, I'm
going to take a vacation

00:05:43.869 --> 00:05:46.861
to a beautiful place called Someday Isle.

00:05:46.861 --> 00:05:49.637
(laughter)

00:05:49.637 --> 00:05:51.793
And in my estimation, 80%
of the population lives

00:05:51.793 --> 00:05:53.446
on Someday Isle.

00:05:53.446 --> 00:05:56.575
Someday I'll lose some weight
and someday I'll read that

00:05:56.575 --> 00:06:00.251
book and listen to that program
and join the Yes Network

00:06:00.251 --> 00:06:02.614
and someday I'll get out of
debt, someday I'll increase

00:06:02.614 --> 00:06:04.861
my income, but it's always someday I'll.

00:06:04.861 --> 00:06:07.276
If you want to be a great
success, there's one simple rule.

00:06:07.276 --> 00:06:11.395
It's vote yourself off
the island, for life.

00:06:11.395 --> 00:06:13.466
If you decide you're going
to do something, do it.

00:06:13.466 --> 00:06:15.229
You know, they've done
dozens and dozens of studies

00:06:15.229 --> 00:06:17.212
over the years, they find that
there's one major difference

00:06:17.212 --> 00:06:19.532
between successful people
and unsuccessful people

00:06:19.532 --> 00:06:21.818
and successful people launch, they start,

00:06:21.818 --> 00:06:23.135
they get on with it, they just do it.

00:06:23.135 --> 00:06:24.987
Unsuccessful people get the same ideas

00:06:24.987 --> 00:06:28.188
and the same information, but
they've always got an excuse

00:06:28.188 --> 00:06:29.357
for not starting.

00:06:29.357 --> 00:06:33.320
- So many people in life, we
all know these guys, right?

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:37.081
They peaked at high school,
they were Prom King,

00:06:37.081 --> 00:06:41.495
they were quarterback of the
'ing team, they go through life

00:06:41.495 --> 00:06:44.036
and you see 'em 10 years
later and they're sitting

00:06:44.036 --> 00:06:47.558
at the bar on a Tuesday with
their male pattern baldness

00:06:47.558 --> 00:06:49.846
and they're like, "Uh,
bro, back in the day

00:06:49.846 --> 00:06:52.980
I was the 'ing man and they
can't pay their 'ing bills,

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:55.372
they're driving a hunk
of and they've turned

00:06:55.372 --> 00:06:58.983
into a basically complete
accelerated version of themselves

00:06:58.983 --> 00:07:02.223
which is a douche bag and
they haven't done anything

00:07:02.223 --> 00:07:03.905
with their lives, right?

00:07:03.905 --> 00:07:05.338
And we see these people all the time

00:07:05.338 --> 00:07:08.951
and the reason these people don't progress

00:07:08.951 --> 00:07:11.987
is because they focus on the glory days.

00:07:11.987 --> 00:07:15.040
They focus on the things they
have achieved in the past

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:19.177
and they don't let themselves
work towards a better future.

00:07:19.177 --> 00:07:22.906
And guys, you have to be
able to look at yourself

00:07:22.906 --> 00:07:25.067
and be honest with yourself on this.

00:07:25.067 --> 00:07:28.808
If this is you, you have to
stop this behavior, okay?

00:07:28.808 --> 00:07:32.975
When you focus no what you
did last year or what you did

00:07:34.342 --> 00:07:36.916
two years ago, or what you did last month,

00:07:36.916 --> 00:07:40.029
or the award I won at the company function

00:07:40.029 --> 00:07:42.875
or the sales numbers that I hit

00:07:42.875 --> 00:07:46.530
and beat everybody on
the squad, or whatever.

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:50.089
When you focus on this
guys, that is energy

00:07:50.089 --> 00:07:53.151
that you could be putting
into actually improving

00:07:53.151 --> 00:07:57.154
and focusing on the task at
hand which is today, okay?

00:07:57.154 --> 00:08:01.321
Champions don't sulk and
Kobe Bryant doesn't sit there

00:08:02.383 --> 00:08:05.081
and talk about how many MVPs he's won

00:08:05.081 --> 00:08:07.204
or how many championships he's won, no.

00:08:07.204 --> 00:08:09.563
The mother's up at three
o'clock in the morning

00:08:09.563 --> 00:08:14.547
practicing everyday, why
do you think he's so great?

00:08:14.547 --> 00:08:16.831
He's not great because
he's great, he's great

00:08:16.831 --> 00:08:19.641
because he puts the 'ing
work in on a daily basis

00:08:19.641 --> 00:08:21.891
and he wins every 'ing day.

00:08:22.752 --> 00:08:24.295
- Our paths are very determinate.

00:08:24.295 --> 00:08:28.165
When you think about Europe
or the western hemisphere

00:08:28.165 --> 00:08:31.725
in general, we are stuck
by issues of the past.

00:08:31.725 --> 00:08:34.343
It is the past that holds back, you know?

00:08:34.343 --> 00:08:38.664
And if you said that you were,
as I've done in the past,

00:08:38.664 --> 00:08:41.021
let me burn everything, let
me get rid of everything

00:08:41.021 --> 00:08:45.178
in the past, you're free to
start thinking about the future.

00:08:45.178 --> 00:08:47.184
But if you're still collecting the past

00:08:47.184 --> 00:08:49.591
and looking to the past as a solution,

00:08:49.591 --> 00:08:53.169
having history is a very strong anchor.

00:08:53.169 --> 00:08:57.122
You're unable to move forward
because there are historical

00:08:57.122 --> 00:09:01.339
reasons why our tribe of
humanity is such a slow changer

00:09:01.339 --> 00:09:04.657
because change is very, very scary

00:09:04.657 --> 00:09:08.072
and human beings don't do
scary things on their own.

00:09:08.072 --> 00:09:12.239
It takes something much bigger
to force them into change.

00:09:15.087 --> 00:09:17.157
- [Man] What kind of
big thing could that be?

00:09:17.157 --> 00:09:21.477
- For every human being
individual, it's the heart attack,

00:09:21.477 --> 00:09:23.959
the car accident, something that happened

00:09:23.959 --> 00:09:26.820
which was much bigger than
you, suddenly you wake up

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:29.313
and say, "Oh my God, I've
been spending all my life

00:09:29.313 --> 00:09:32.176
inside a box just
working for someone else.

00:09:32.176 --> 00:09:34.112
Oh, isn't there a better way?"

00:09:34.112 --> 00:09:37.585
For humanity in general, it is this.

00:09:37.585 --> 00:09:41.428
Suddenly it stops raining,
suddenly everything goes crazy

00:09:41.428 --> 00:09:44.830
and you can't control the
climate, so that's big enough.

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:48.086
If the world were hit by a
meteorite, it will be enough.

00:09:48.086 --> 00:09:51.867
It takes enormous things
like that so we are dinosaurs

00:09:51.867 --> 00:09:55.179
in that sense, we roam
around and do our thing

00:09:55.179 --> 00:09:58.349
until we're hit by something
much bigger than us.

00:09:58.349 --> 00:10:00.429
And that's true even for
the individual who needs

00:10:00.429 --> 00:10:02.159
a heart attack to wake up to find out

00:10:02.159 --> 00:10:03.645
that they've been working too much.

